			"Message": "build(deps): bump pnpm/action-setup from 4.2.0 to 5.0.0\n\nBumps [pnpm/action-setup](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup) from 4.2.0 to 5.0.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/compare/v4.2.0...v5.0.0)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: pnpm/action-setup\n  dependency-version: 5.0.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "b5e7cf04ddd1045287e1400e41ee8986f1c4a30a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-13T07:47:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				68,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Worker): Add .gitignore to exclude build artifacts\n\nThis commit adds a .gitignore file to the Worker element, preventing ephemeral build artifacts from being committed to the repository. The configuration excludes the Target/ directory (build outputs), Configuration/ (build scripts), and standard development files such as node_modules, environment files, logs, and IDE-specific directories.\n\nThis ensures a clean repository state, reducing noise in the git history and preventing accidental commits of build artifacts. The only exception is preserving Target/debug and Target/release folders, which may be needed for specific build configurations or debugging scenarios.",
			"SHA": "14232fb488533251ad2a832fd043296fdd4481d7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-13T03:39:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				67,
				12
			],
			"Message": "build(Worker): Restore development-readable build artifacts with source maps\n\nThis commit reverts the minification applied in the previous commit for the Worker element, expanding the build artifacts back to development-readable formats with full source map support.\n\nKey changes:\n- Configuration/ESBuild/Target.js expanded from 1 line to 24 lines, adding helper functions (__defProp, __name) and proper named exports\n- Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js expanded from 1 line to 54 lines, revealing the full esbuild configuration with the Target plugin setup logic\n- Target/Worker.js increased from ~2.6KB to ~10.3KB (4x larger)\n- Target/Worker/CSS/Load.js increased from ~335 bytes to ~1.1KB (3.5x larger)\n- Target/Worker/Policy.js increased from ~513 bytes to ~2.1KB (4x larger)\n- Target/Worker/Register.js increased from ~1.3KB to ~5.1KB (4x larger)\n- All source map files (.js.map) have been regenerated and added back\n\nThis change enables debugging of the Service Worker in development mode, providing better visibility into the asset caching, offline support, and dynamic CSS loading implementations within the Land editor's webview.",
			"SHA": "338d634ff6b0e55642b6f3f12381645528dafead"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-11T02:21:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				61,
				13
			],
			"Message": "build(Worker): Minify Service Worker build artifacts for production\n\nThis commit applies minification to the Worker element's build outputs, transitioning from development-readable formats to production-optimized versions.\n\nKey changes:\n- Configuration/ESBuild/Target.js and Worker.js have been minified from 24/54 lines respectively to single-line representations\n- Target/Worker.js (main Service Worker entry) reduced from ~10KB to ~2.6KB\n- Target/Worker/CSS/Load.js reduced from ~1.1KB to ~335 bytes\n- Target/Worker/Policy.js reduced from ~2.1KB to ~513 bytes\n- Target/Worker/Register.js reduced from ~5.1KB to ~1.3KB\n- All .js.map source map files have been deleted to reduce bundle size\n\nAdditionally, a minor documentation fix in README.md corrects the License section formatting.\n\nThis optimization ensures smaller payload sizes for the Service Worker, improving load times for the Land editor's webview while maintaining full functionality for asset caching, offline support, and dynamic CSS loading.",
			"SHA": "4d1f36deb9a72d342a650cb68a6e59218ff11bc0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "dependabot[bot]",
			"Date": "2026-03-04T05:53:52Z",
